E mergency (E ntry Visa) Checklist

• If you ever held an Indian Passport, it is MANDATORY to provide proof of the Renunciation of Indian Citizenship along with your VISA application. One of the following MUST be produced as proof: - ❖ Certificate of renunciation issued by the Embassy/Consulate of India OR ❖ Deemed surrender certificate issued by the Embassy/Consulate of India Both - Cancelled/ Surrendered Passport along with the copy of the Surrender/Renunciation Certificate would be needed for Indian passports surrendered after May 2010 If you do not have the proof of renunciation, then please apply for renunciation before submitting the VISA application PROOF OF INDIAN ORIGIN- COPY
• If the applicant was an Indian national: Indian passport of the applicant;
• If the applicant is a child of an Indian national, Person of Indian Origin or OCI Cardholder: Birth certificate of the applicant together with Indian passport or OCI Card of either parent;
• If the applicant is the ‘Spouse of Foreign Origin’ of an Indian national, Person of Indian Origin or OCI Cardholder: Marriage certificate of the applicant together with Indian passport or OCI Card of the spouse.

